# The SPA itself needs NO build-time env vars.
#
# In the BFF model the frontend has no knowledge of Keycloak — all auth goes
# through the backend on the SAME origin, at its own unrewritten paths:
#   GET  /api/v1/auth/login     — backend redirects the browser to Keycloak
#   GET  /api/v1/auth/callback  — Keycloak posts the user back (path-scoped cookie!)
#   POST /api/v1/auth/logout    — terminates the server-side session
#   GET  /api/v1/auth/me        — current user (from the session, never a token)
# The browser only ever holds an opaque HttpOnly session cookie.
#
# `npm run dev` proxies /api/v1 → http://localhost:8000 (vite.config.ts). Nothing to set.

# --- Only for `docker compose up` (see docker-compose.yml) ---
# Where nginx proxies /api/v1. Required by the compose file, unused by npm scripts.
BACKEND_UPSTREAM=https://ba-dev.example.com
# Host port for the served SPA (default 3000).
#FRONTEND_PORT=3000
